        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Dublin</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 841 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> settlement of about 841 called Dyflin, beside a Christian ecclesiastical settlement known as Duibhlinn; a Gaelic settlement, Áth Cliath, stood further up the river. The Irish government recognised 988 as the year of the city's settlement.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On Dublin Bay at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-liffey">River Liffey</a> in the province of Leinster, on the east coast of Ireland, with the Dublin Mountains to the south.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> town of Dyflin; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin-castle">Dublin Castle</a>, founded in 1204; Trinity College, founded in 1592; Georgian Dublin and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wide-streets-commission">Wide Streets Commission</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-ireland">Parliament of Ireland</a> until 1800; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-rising">Easter Rising</a> of 1916; the Guinness brewery; the capital of the Irish Free State</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Dublin is the capital and largest city of Ireland and the seat of its parliament, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oireachtas">Oireachtas</a>.</span></div>
